ers","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/red/v1/transporte/buffers#relación-con-tnet","content":"`Buffer` es la evolución renombrada de `TNBuffer`. La arquitectura de pool, lectura/escritura y reciclado procede de TNet, mientras que la nomenclatura de Eco es la API utilizada por Pandora."},"574":{"id":"/docs/red/v1/transporte/buffers-37","page_id":"/docs/red/v1/transporte/buffers","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/red/v1/transporte/buffers#relación-con-tnet","content":"Implementación del buffer binario."},"575":{"id":"/docs/red/v1/transporte/buffers-38","page_id":"/docs/red/v1/transporte/buffers","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/red/v1/transporte/buffers#relación-con-tnet","content":"Repositorio upstream."},"576":{"id":"/docs/red/v1/transporte","page_id":"/docs/red/v1/transporte","type":"page","content":"Transporte","breadcrumbs":["Docs","Red","Red","Contenido","Transporte"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/red/v1/transporte"},"577":{"id":"/docs/red/v1/transporte-0","page_id":"/docs/red/v1/transporte","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/red/v1/transporte","content":"Cómo Eco empaqueta, serializa y transporta datos entre clientes y servidor."},"578":{"id":"/docs/red/v1/transporte-1","page_id":"/docs/red/v1/transporte","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/red/v1/transporte#transporte","content":"Transporte"},"579":{"id":"/docs/red/v1/transporte-2","page_id":"/docs/red/v1/transporte","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/red/v1/transporte#transporte","content":"Esta sección describe las capas que convierten una operación de red en datos transmisibles y los mecanismos que los llevan entre cliente y servidor."},"580":{"id":"/docs/red/v1/transporte-3","page_id":"/docs/red/v1/transporte","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/red/v1/transporte#transporte","content":"Tipos de mensaje y protocolo de Eco."},"581":{"id":"/docs/red/v1/transporte-4","page_id":"/docs/red/v1/transporte","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/red/v1/transporte#transporte","content":"Lectura, escritura